      "body": "> Would you take a pull request that sets `permissions: contents: read` and `persist-credentials: false`, and pins actions and images by full SHA or digest with version comments?\n\nConcept ACK\n\nSome defense-in-depth hardening won't hurt here, in particular if it's as simple as adding a `permission` block with two entries. Workflow permissions are set to \"Read repository contents and packages permissions\" but it sounds like a good idea to make it explicit in the yaml (if only for forks).\n\nBut we should keep this in sync with whatever best practices Bitcoin Core applies here. cc @hebasto @fanquake \n\n",
